  SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
  Author Claude/bentzn

  The HTTP half: the discovery document, the token endpoint, the OpenID Connect
  browser flow, the mint and the admin surface. It adds an HTTP surface to
  oidc-core; it encodes no JWK of its own.

  THE SOURCES CAME FROM `basenet/shared/jwtmint`, NOT FROM `raposza/apps/jwtmint`
  - measured 2026-09-19. BaseNet's copy is the strict superset: it carries the
  browser flow that the Sandbox's copy does not have at all, and it already
  carries the port correction that leaves about forty stale `33301` mentions in
  the Raposza copy. R-11 feared the copy would fall BEHIND; it went ahead.

  THE REPACKAGE EXECUTION ID IS `repackage` AND THAT IS NOT COSMETIC.
  spring-boot-starter-parent already declares an execution of that id in its
  pluginManagement, so an execution under any OTHER id does not override it -
  it is added beside it, and the module gets two repackages. The first rewrites
  the plain jar in place with Main-Class = JarLauncher; the second reads that
  jar, takes JarLauncher for the application's own main class, and writes it as
  Start-Class. The result launches itself for ever:

    JarLauncher.main -> Launcher.launch -> Class.forName
      -> JarLauncher.main -> ... -> StackOverflowError

  Nothing in the build says so. `mvn package` is green, the jar is the right
  size, and the failure arrives only when it is run. Matching the id merges the
  two into one.

  mainClass is stated for the same reason: the parent configures it as
  ${start-class}, a property this module does not set.

  CLASSIFIER `app`, so the runnable jar and the plain one have different names
  rather than being the same name at different times - which is what a launcher
  that finds its jar by glob depends on.

  THE REPACKAGE IS UNCONDITIONAL, not behind a profile. In this tree the
  runnable jar IS the deliverable; `apps/jwtmint` put it behind `-Papp` because
  it sat inside a reactor whose gate reached the package phase on every run.
-->
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <parent>
        <groupId>com.raposza.oidc</groupId>
        <artifactId>raposza-oidc</artifactId>
        <version>0.3.0</version>
    </parent>

    <artifactId>raposza-oidc-server</artifactId>
    <name>Raposza OIDC - server</name>
    <description>The HTTP half of Raposza OIDC: discovery, JWKS, the token endpoint, the OpenID Connect browser flow, the mint, the admin surface and the web UI.</description>

    <dependencies>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>com.raposza.oidc</groupId>
            <artifactId>raposza-oidc-core</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>com.nimbusds</groupId>
            <artifactId>nimbus-jose-jwt</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <!-- Swagger UI and the OpenAPI document, generated from the
             controllers rather than hand-written beside them. A specification
             maintained by hand is a specification that is wrong within a week,
             and this API is the one a caller has to read before it can ask for
             anything. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springdoc</groupId>
            <artifactId>springdoc-openapi-starter-webmvc-ui</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-test</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>

    <build>
        <plugins>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-source-plugin</artifactId>
            </plugin>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-javadoc-plugin</artifactId>
            </plugin>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
                <artifactId>spring-boot-maven-plugin</artifactId>
                <executions>
                    <execution>
                        <id>repackage</id>
                        <goals>
                            <goal>repackage</goal>
                        </goals>
                        <configuration>
                            <classifier>app</classifier>
                            <mainClass>com.raposza.oidc.OidcApp</mainClass>
                        </configuration>
                    </execution>
                </executions>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>

</project>
